\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces BudgetPredictor outcome during fine-tuning of the warm-started checkpoint. Collapse: $k_{\mathrm  {eff}}{>}0.99\,k_{\max }$ for $\geq 2$K consecutive steps. $k_{\mathrm  {eff}}$ is the final effective budget; Val is best observed validation NTP loss, not a direct selector-quality ranking because token counts and continuation trajectories differ. Seed-7 replications are completed for $\lambda _b\in \{0.03,0.08,0.10,0.15\}$; ``n/a'' indicates not replicated in seed~7. Collapse denotes saturation to the full-budget policy: the low Val at seed-7 $\lambda _b{=}0.03$ shows that a collapsed head can still behave as a strong fixed-full-budget model, but it eliminates per-sample token reduction below $k_{\max }$. Stronger budget pressure means non-collapsed $k_{\mathrm  {eff}}$ below $k_{\max }$ with worse Val than the best stable setting; $\lambda _b{=}0.20$ remains exploratory and single-seed.}}{8}{table.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:budget-collapse}{{1}{8}{BudgetPredictor outcome during fine-tuning of the warm-started checkpoint. Collapse: $\keff {>}0.99\,\kmax $ for $\geq 2$K consecutive steps. $\keff $ is the final effective budget; Val is best observed validation NTP loss, not a direct selector-quality ranking because token counts and continuation trajectories differ. Seed-7 replications are completed for $\lbb \in \{0.03,0.08,0.10,0.15\}$; ``n/a'' indicates not replicated in seed~7. Collapse denotes saturation to the full-budget policy: the low Val at seed-7 $\lbb {=}0.03$ shows that a collapsed head can still behave as a strong fixed-full-budget model, but it eliminates per-sample token reduction below $\kmax $. Stronger budget pressure means non-collapsed $\keff $ below $\kmax $ with worse Val than the best stable setting; $\lbb {=}0.20$ remains exploratory and single-seed}{table.caption.16}{}}
